0..73 Comment "//! The null niche as a realizability predicate. A type\'s realisers are a"
74..155 Comment "//! predicate on a word and a heap, `V⟦T⟧ : (Nat, Heap) => Type`; the heap is"
156..236 Comment "//! data, the separating conjunction a sigma over a disjoint split and points-to"
237..311 Comment "//! a singleton, so the normaliser computes every assertion and the kernel"
312..346 Comment "//! replays every declaration here"
347..427 Comment "//! [Wagner-2024-realistic_realizability_specifying_abis_you_can_count], § 4.2."
428..507 Comment "//! `Option<&T>` is one word, null or a reference; its realisers are equivalent"
508..585 Comment "//! at every heap to those of the two-word tagged layout, and the marshallers"
586..657 Comment "//! between the two meet their triples. A C function specified by hand,"
658..734 Comment "//! `deref_or`, is met by the niche; its `_Nonnull` neighbour is refused, in"
735..800 Comment "//! `../../pathological/specification/niche-realizability.gandr`."
801..804 Comment "//!"
805..879 Comment "//! Words are `Nat`, null `Zero`, so a case on a word reduces; a triple is"
880..950 Comment "//! `P(h) => wp(c, Q, h)`, and a pure marshaller\'s precondition is its"
951..1029 Comment "//! postcondition at its answer. Departing from § 4.2: both layouts are words"
1030..1103 Comment "//! by value rather than objects behind a reference count, so there is no"
1104..1182 Comment "//! `size` and no count; there is no later modality; and a triple is stated at"
1183..1257 Comment "//! the heap it owns, with no frame rule over it. Where a realiser runs to"
1258..1299 Comment "//! `emp(h)` the proofs case on the heap."
1300..1303 Comment "//!"
1304..1320 Comment "//! - see: #2832"
1321..1352 Comment "//! - see: #327 — `derefOrWp`"
1353..1433 Comment "//! - cites: [Wagner-2024-realistic_realizability_specifying_abis_you_can_count]"
1434..1437 Comment "//!"
1438..1629 Comment "//! [Wagner-2024-realistic_realizability_specifying_abis_you_can_count]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3689755 \"Wagner, Eisbach and Ahmed, Realistic Realizability: Specifying ABIs You Can Count On\""
